1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,260
One girl transforms, now bright, kind, and cheerful, but someone else changes too, into something dark, fierce, and cruel.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:59,980
One girl transforms, now bright, kind, and cheerful, but someone else changes too.

3
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:29,960
One girl transforms, now bright, kind, and cheerful, but someone else changes too.

4
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:36,960
One girl transforms, now bright, kind, and cheerful, but someone else changes too.

5
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:43,960
One girl transforms, now bright, kind, and cheerful, but someone else changes too.

6
00:01:44,960 --> 00:01:49,220
I'm sorry, did it happen again?

7
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:51,460
Did what happen?

8
00:01:51,720 --> 00:01:56,860
Nothing, my apologies. Lately I've been having these blackout moments where my mind goes blank.

9
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,960
It goes blank, as in...

10
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:02,920
It's nothing to worry about, I'm probably anemic or something.

11
00:02:03,620 --> 00:02:07,340
Anyway, I guess you read your note, the one I left on your desk?

12
00:02:07,340 --> 00:02:10,260
Uh, yeah, are you still free on Saturday?

13
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:12,320
Oh, sorry, there's somewhere I have to be.

14
00:02:15,020 --> 00:02:17,640
Kurumi, you can stop hiding now.

15
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:20,620
You know me too well.

16
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:22,100
Crazy, huh?

17
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:26,980
This really does make it a lot harder to understand why origami turned inverse, wouldn't you say?

18
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:31,940
Yeah, but this origami was able to accept the death of her parents.

19
00:02:32,660 --> 00:02:34,620
I don't get it. What happened?

20
00:02:34,620 --> 00:02:37,920
Let me see if I've got this straight.

21
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:43,000
So you're saying, this world exists because you used Kurumi's time travel powers,

22
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:46,820
and you did that to save origami's parents who should have died five years ago,

23
00:02:46,940 --> 00:02:49,980
and the purpose of that was to avoid what she would have turned into.

24
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:52,220
Yeah, that's the gist of it.

25
00:02:52,620 --> 00:02:54,220
Hmm, fascinating.

26
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:58,880
I think now I get why you've been acting a little strange for the last day or so.

27
00:02:59,380 --> 00:03:02,980
It's true. Maybe origami shouldn't have inversed in this world.

28
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:07,700
Regardless, she definitely did, and now we have devil to contend with.

29
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:11,340
I've analyzed her encounter with Shin on the roof.

30
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:12,960
He's telling the truth.

31
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:18,360
Believe it or not, origami Tobiichi hasn't the faintest idea that she's a spirit.

32
00:03:18,380 --> 00:03:19,360
But how can that be?

33
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:22,600
Shin, you managed to change the course of time.

34
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:27,860
So you and Kurumi are the only ones with actual knowledge of the original world, correct?

35
00:03:27,980 --> 00:03:28,400
Yeah.

36
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:34,680
And as for Kurumi, considering her own powers are what brought this about, she's kind of an exception.

37
00:03:35,580 --> 00:03:40,180
So if I had to guess from everything you've told me, in order to retain knowledge of the original world,

38
00:03:40,660 --> 00:03:42,060
two conditions must be met.

39
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:47,460
Being directly hit by Kurumi's yudbet, and having spirit powers flowing through oneself.

40
00:03:47,460 --> 00:03:54,800
With both conditions met, it's possible that one's memory of the original world may be recovered.

41
00:03:55,640 --> 00:04:00,300
We know that origami was shot by Kurumi's yudbet, so the first condition was met.

42
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:04,620
Separately, she's ended up living a peaceful life thanks to Shido's interference.

43
00:04:04,620 --> 00:04:09,620
But then, when phantom showed up on the scene and gave her spirit powers...

44
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:12,300
She finally remembered everything.

45
00:04:13,740 --> 00:04:17,960
However, as a self-defense mechanism, her memories were split in two.

46
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:24,160
Essentially, there's one origami who lives in peace, and then there's the spirit hunter, devil.

47
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:31,820
So now, as soon as origami senses spirit power, she loses control of her mind and memory.

48
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:34,420
And then, the inverse version of her is awakened.

49
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:37,660
The theory works and is consistent with what we know.

50
00:04:37,940 --> 00:04:40,360
The question is, what can we do about it?

51
00:04:40,460 --> 00:04:44,380
As long as origami's a spirit, there's only one thing for Rattata Skirt to do.

52
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:47,460
Make her fall for me, right?

53
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:48,300
Correct.

54
00:04:48,300 --> 00:04:50,740
That's how we'll seal her spirit powers.

55
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,900
You'll need to convince origami to go out on a date with you.

56
00:04:54,140 --> 00:04:56,040
Think you can handle that, lover boy?

57
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,520
What now? Is there a problem?

58
00:04:58,860 --> 00:05:01,180
Nothing. It's just...

59
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:04,460
Huh? You've already promised to meet up with her this Saturday?

60
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:07,200
So you hit on her before even knowing that she was a spirit?

61
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:08,060
The heck?

62
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:08,860
Dude.

63
00:05:09,340 --> 00:05:11,840
Well, I mean, it's complicated.

64
00:05:18,300 --> 00:05:20,740
I can't believe I wrote him a note.

65
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:24,420
Since when did I become some kind of lovesick girly girl?

66
00:05:26,460 --> 00:05:27,560
I don't know.

67
00:05:27,980 --> 00:05:29,560
Maybe it's...

68
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:32,800
It's from him!

69
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:41,400
Okay. Got a reply.

70
00:05:41,860 --> 00:05:44,140
Yes, thank you. That time and date will work for me.

71
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:45,840
Is that too impersonal?

72
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:50,220
Dear Itsuka, as I write this, the winds of autumn fill me with hope and anticipation.

73
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:54,680
And the moon sits like a big egg in the sky as I wonder how you're faring tonight.

74
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:57,640
Who says that? No one!

75
00:05:57,640 --> 00:06:07,560
I really appreciate you inviting me here today, Itsuka.

76
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:09,880
You okay?

77
00:06:10,660 --> 00:06:11,840
Yeah, my pleasure.

78
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:16,200
Since we're hanging out, could we maybe do first names now, pretty please?

79
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:17,680
Oh, of course we can.

80
00:06:19,220 --> 00:06:20,160
Sounds good.

81
00:06:21,520 --> 00:06:23,520
That's more like the origami, I know.

82
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,000
Sorry, too fast?

83
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:26,780
Guess I'm just anxious to say your name.

84
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:28,220
I mean, cause it's so pretty.

85
00:06:28,460 --> 00:06:29,060
Thank you.

86
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:32,160
I've always been glad my parents picked it for me.

87
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:36,040
If you like calling me that so much, say it as often as you want.

88
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:37,480
I don't mind at all.

89
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:40,000
Feel free to call me Shido, too.

90
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:42,220
Thanks. I'll work up the courage soon.

91
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:44,440
Kill me now. This is unbearable.

92
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,120
So, what do you think we should do today?

93
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:48,360
Good question.

94
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:52,180
Here we go.

95
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:53,540
Your choices, everyone.

96
00:06:53,540 --> 00:06:57,680
Mm-hmm. That seems right to me.

97
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:02,680
I hated to pass up the first choice, but going someplace where they can't talk is a pretty classic blunder.

98
00:07:03,100 --> 00:07:05,800
Plus, choice number two is a safe and versatile option.

99
00:07:06,120 --> 00:07:08,560
Even if she isn't into shopping, they'll have lots of fun.

100
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:11,720
All right, Shido. We're ready. Go with you.

101
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:12,340
Hold up a sec.

102
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:14,780
I want to test out a different choice.

103
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:16,420
Oh, yeah!

104
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:21,960
Emotional levels are unstable.

105
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:24,560
Origami Tobiichi is distraught.

106
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:27,220
Big shocker there?

107
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:28,920
What are you thinking, Shido?

108
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:30,500
Talk your way out of it!

109
00:07:30,580 --> 00:07:31,480
Right. I will.

110
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:33,800
Sorry about that. Wrong building.

111
00:07:34,020 --> 00:07:35,180
Oh, so that wasn't it.

112
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:35,740
Okay.

113
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:39,420
Man, I genuinely thought Origami would go crazy for that.

114
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:41,220
You never cease to amaze me.

115
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:42,880
Look, just go with two, okay?

116
00:07:43,140 --> 00:07:44,160
Take the girls shopping.

117
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:45,300
Roger.

118
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:47,660
Break it gently. How's her happiness level?

119
00:07:48,180 --> 00:07:49,960
I hope it didn't drop too drastically.

120
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:51,160
Yeah, about that.

121
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:53,520
Her emotions are bouncing all over the place,

122
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:55,760
but her happiness actually seems to be rising.

123
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:57,200
Are you serious?

124
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:59,280
Hey, where are we going to go shopping?

125
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:01,360
Um, let's see.

126
00:08:03,380 --> 00:08:04,780
Your choices, everyone.

127
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:07,580
It's got to be the third one.

128
00:08:07,980 --> 00:08:08,340
Huh?

129
00:08:08,820 --> 00:08:10,520
Have you lost your damn mind?

130
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:13,040
No way can you take a girl there on the first date.

131
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:16,740
Yeah, but Origami and Everdegex go together like peanut butter and jelly.

132
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:18,300
Wait, you know what I'm saying, right?

133
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:22,040
Origami, this way.

134
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:28,080
Here we are.

135
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:28,920
What do you think?

136
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:34,060
I'm so sorry, Itsuka, but I have to admit,

137
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:36,700
I don't even know what most of the stuff in here is.

138
00:08:36,900 --> 00:08:38,480
Yeah, right? Very funny.

139
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:41,060
Then what's all that?

140
00:08:41,060 --> 00:08:41,440
Huh?

141
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:45,720
What? What's going on?

142
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:47,120
Why do I have all this?

143
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:49,660
I don't understand what's the matter with me.

144
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:51,600
What made me pick up those things?

145
00:08:51,860 --> 00:08:52,840
Don't worry about it.

146
00:08:53,220 --> 00:08:56,320
It's totally my fault for taking you to the store in the first place.

147
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:59,740
How would you feel about a new outfit as my way of apologizing?

148
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:00,740
That sound good?

149
00:09:01,060 --> 00:09:02,940
What? No, I can't let you do that.

150
00:09:03,020 --> 00:09:04,420
Please don't worry, I got it.

151
00:09:04,420 --> 00:09:08,960
In exchange, all I ask is that you let me be the first to see you wearing it.

152
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:11,320
That's the only payment I need.

153
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:13,180
Tell me something.

154
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:15,140
Are you kind of a ladies' man?

155
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:17,140
You're almost too good at this.

156
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:17,820
No!

157
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:19,220
No, it's not true at all!

158
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:21,360
Then I guess I'll take you up on that offer.

159
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:26,580
And while I'm at it, I should make sure it's an outfit that you'll like a whole lot.

160
00:09:29,260 --> 00:09:30,700
You ladies' man.

161
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:32,700
She really called you out, didn't she?

162
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:33,920
Yeah, not helpful.

163
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:34,500
Shut up.

164
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:37,020
Hey, I don't remember saying it was a bad thing.

165
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:40,980
Shin, Origami just went into a dressing room in the back of the store.

166
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:42,640
Don't lose sight of her.

167
00:09:42,820 --> 00:09:43,560
Right, thanks.

168
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:46,000
Origami!

169
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,140
Are you okay?

170
00:09:48,420 --> 00:09:49,180
I...

171
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:50,300
What am I doing?

172
00:09:50,780 --> 00:09:51,260
Sorry.

173
00:09:51,740 --> 00:09:52,760
I'm coming in!

174
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:53,820
No, please don't!

175
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:03,020
So, let me ask.

176
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:06,840
Did you pick this because you thought for some reason that I'd be into it?

177
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:07,640
I don't know!

178
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:08,960
That's why I freaked out!

179
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:12,680
I mean, I don't even remember taking these clothes off the rack!

180
00:10:14,040 --> 00:10:15,020
I'm sorry.

181
00:10:15,020 --> 00:10:16,060
Again.

182
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:19,400
For some reason, I'm weird today.

183
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:21,240
Don't let it bother you.

184
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:23,260
Nothing you've said or done has fazed me.

185
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:25,340
Thanks for that.

186
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:28,740
Sorry, bathroom break.

187
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:29,920
I'll be right back.

188
00:10:30,580 --> 00:10:31,880
Sure, go ahead.

189
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:31,960
Oh.

190
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:35,440
Oh.

191
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:39,960
Oh.

192
00:10:45,020 --> 00:10:47,140
So sorry to keep you waiting like that.

193
00:10:51,780 --> 00:10:52,260
Hey.

194
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:53,460
What you doing?

195
00:10:56,280 --> 00:10:56,760
No.

196
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:57,220
Wait.

197
00:10:57,300 --> 00:10:58,720
This isn't whatever you're thinking right now.

198
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:01,280
Your spoon fell off the table, so I was just picking it up.

199
00:11:01,280 --> 00:11:04,660
I'm so sorry.

200
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:05,900
It's nothing.

201
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:06,620
Don't sweat it.

202
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:08,960
It'll dry in no time.

203
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:13,660
What are you doing?

204
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:17,000
Why am I...

205
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:18,040
You have to believe me.

206
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:20,360
It's like my body's moving all on its own.

207
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:22,180
What is going on with me?

208
00:11:22,180 --> 00:11:22,780
Oh.

209
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:30,620
Origami Tobiichi's emotional levels have now stabilized.

210
00:11:31,460 --> 00:11:33,340
Her happiness meter still remains high.

211
00:11:34,140 --> 00:11:35,520
The mood isn't bad either.

212
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:37,960
With any luck, we could wrap this up in one day.

213
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:39,400
Perhaps.

214
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:42,640
However, it seems clear that she remains anxious about something.

215
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:46,520
It could just be basic nerves regarding whether Shin will accept her or not.

216
00:11:46,520 --> 00:11:48,480
I'm not surprised after all she did.

217
00:11:49,260 --> 00:11:51,940
I feel like it should only take one more push, though.

218
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:52,840
Seriously?

219
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:55,600
So, you mean you're done with the AST, then?

220
00:11:56,820 --> 00:12:00,900
My anemia and those blackout moments are both pretty solid reasons to quit.

221
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:03,580
Also, I just don't know anymore.

222
00:12:04,860 --> 00:12:06,460
Is it really the right thing to do?

223
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:09,300
Continuing to wipe out spirits the way that I have?

224
00:12:10,700 --> 00:12:11,560
Forgive me.

225
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:15,820
I forgot it was a spirit that was responsible for the death of your brother, too.

226
00:12:15,820 --> 00:12:17,880
You don't have to be sorry for that.

227
00:12:18,920 --> 00:12:22,800
Listen, I think you're very smart to question it, and I completely agree with you.

228
00:12:23,100 --> 00:12:26,120
And to be totally honest, my brother would say the same thing.

229
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:27,820
Oh, my sweet friend.

230
00:12:28,340 --> 00:12:29,400
I'm so sorry.

231
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:32,020
Thank you for telling me that.

232
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:34,920
Happiness meter climbing!

233
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:36,900
Maximum value has been reached!

234
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:38,100
Hmm.

235
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:41,080
That must have been the source of her earlier anxiety.

236
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:43,080
So now it seems she's turned a corner.

237
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:43,960
Shido!

238
00:12:44,280 --> 00:12:45,200
It's looking good!

239
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:48,000
I'd say it's time for you to dive in for the kill!

240
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:58,260
We're coming!

241
00:13:03,260 --> 00:13:08,160
Are you all right?

242
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:08,920
You hurt?

243
00:13:09,340 --> 00:13:09,780
No.

244
00:13:09,780 --> 00:13:11,780
Shido, I'm...

245
00:13:11,780 --> 00:13:13,780
Shido, I'm...

246
00:13:13,780 --> 00:13:22,460
Origami, are you okay?

247
00:13:22,460 --> 00:13:22,480
You okay?

248
00:13:32,980 --> 00:13:33,780
Spirit...

249
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:38,980
No, her spirit power.

250
00:13:38,980 --> 00:13:40,560
Shido, get out of there!

251
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:42,680
Origami?

252
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:50,300
What was that?

253
00:13:50,300 --> 00:14:03,820
What's that?

254
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:04,820
What am I sensing?

255
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:05,940
Shiver.

256
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:07,340
My heart is restless.

257
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:08,600
There, look!

258
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:13,720
What are you thinking?

259
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:18,660
What are you thinking?

260
00:14:18,880 --> 00:14:19,820
It's too dangerous!

261
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:21,740
Origami is after me now!

262
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:25,220
Our only chance to steal her is to do it while her armor is incomplete!

263
00:14:25,220 --> 00:14:34,520
If I run away, the city will be demolished.

264
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:37,020
I can't let her...

265
00:14:37,020 --> 00:14:38,460
Not again.

266
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:39,780
Never again!

267
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:42,020
Shido, stay back!

268
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:45,420
Hydrofolium!

269
00:14:45,420 --> 00:14:50,580
We should be able to use Fraxinus' main battery to break her spirit barrier for three seconds.

270
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:53,800
You'll have to use that chance to get close and steal her...

271
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:55,280
No, Kodori, run!

272
00:14:57,500 --> 00:14:58,260
Kodori!

273
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:07,560
Please, no.

274
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:08,540
Not again.

275
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:11,160
Origami!

276
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:11,240
Origami!

277
00:15:15,420 --> 00:15:17,760
Toka!

278
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:19,540
You all right, Shido?

279
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:21,040
We're here to help!

280
00:15:21,780 --> 00:15:23,040
You guys...

281
00:15:27,120 --> 00:15:32,220
Shido, fill us in.

282
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:33,240
Who the heck is that?

283
00:15:33,360 --> 00:15:35,040
I sense a dreadful spirit power.

284
00:15:35,340 --> 00:15:35,840
You're right.

285
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:37,140
That's Origami.

286
00:15:37,360 --> 00:15:38,420
The transfer student?

287
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:40,640
It's far too dangerous to fight her.

288
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:43,240
I should probably tell you all to run away.

289
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:47,320
But I am begging you to help me save her anyway.

290
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:50,180
Well, isn't that obvious?

291
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:53,440
After all, you're the one who saved me.

292
00:15:53,760 --> 00:15:55,540
You're the one who made my world possible.

293
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:59,500
So this time, it's finally my turn to help you.

294
00:16:01,100 --> 00:16:02,660
Thank you, everyone.

295
00:16:03,740 --> 00:16:04,900
Wait for me, Origami.

296
00:16:04,900 --> 00:16:10,100
Where am I?

297
00:16:10,740 --> 00:16:11,900
Did I lose...

298
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:13,520
Consciousness again?

299
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:15,920
I thought I was just with Itsuka.

300
00:16:18,920 --> 00:16:19,900
Are you...

301
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:22,840
Me?

302
00:16:27,080 --> 00:16:28,320
I don't get it.

303
00:16:28,580 --> 00:16:29,420
What is this?

304
00:16:29,420 --> 00:16:36,660
Oh, my gosh.

305
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:38,420
Are these...

306
00:16:39,380 --> 00:16:40,260
My memories?

307
00:16:40,260 --> 00:16:59,300
We'll distract her, Tio.

308
00:16:59,520 --> 00:16:59,820
Go!

309
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:01,000
Suggestion.

310
00:17:01,140 --> 00:17:02,160
Get out while you can.

311
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:02,860
That's it.

312
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:04,040
Great job, you two.

313
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:06,720
We call Gabriel.

314
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:06,920
Gabriel!

315
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:08,200
Rondo!

316
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:08,700
Rondo!

317
00:17:12,080 --> 00:17:13,040
And march!

318
00:17:16,040 --> 00:17:17,580
What the heck, Matsumi?

319
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:19,580
Why do you have to be such a copycat?

320
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:21,500
I've just always wanted to try that.

321
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:23,540
Here we go!

322
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:33,880
At this rate, he can't even get close to her.

323
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:34,960
Huh?

324
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:39,680
Shida, you've got to reach her!

325
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:40,800
Thank you!

326
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:41,760
Shiriyan!

327
00:17:42,620 --> 00:17:43,420
Yoshida!

328
00:17:47,760 --> 00:17:47,780
Ah!

329
00:17:47,780 --> 00:17:55,120
Now's your chance! Move!

330
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:56,960
Go save the transfer students!

331
00:17:57,040 --> 00:17:58,220
You guys are the best!

332
00:17:58,600 --> 00:17:59,420
We're incoming!

333
00:18:06,420 --> 00:18:08,120
No! Let me in there!

334
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:09,820
Let me in!

335
00:18:11,260 --> 00:18:12,500
Open your heart!

336
00:18:12,980 --> 00:18:13,840
We're incoming!

337
00:18:13,840 --> 00:18:18,060
You're looking at the one who killed your mom and dad.

338
00:18:18,460 --> 00:18:20,880
It's not true! That never happened in this world!

339
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:23,600
Because Itsuka's brother...

340
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:25,880
Now, Itsuka saved them.

341
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:27,560
And what about my memories, huh?

342
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:31,220
Do you think I can ever take back the truth that I killed them?

343
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:32,840
But that's...

344
00:18:38,840 --> 00:18:41,160
I am you, and you are me.

345
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:45,820
And even if the world's remade, the memories will remain, always.

346
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:56,080
There's no hope in the world for me now.

347
00:18:56,460 --> 00:18:58,240
And that means, you too.

348
00:18:58,300 --> 00:18:58,940
Stop! Enough!

349
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:00,760
Please, just stop!

350
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:03,320
I can't... I can't do this!

351
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:08,320
Please...

352
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:08,980
Please...

353
00:19:08,980 --> 00:19:09,980
Somebody...

354
00:19:09,980 --> 00:19:11,980
Somebody please help me!

355
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:14,360
Origami!

356
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:18,320
Origami!

357
00:19:18,620 --> 00:19:19,460
Can you hear me?

358
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:20,220
Itsuka?

359
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:21,700
What the...

360
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:23,140
What is Shiro doing here?

361
00:19:23,380 --> 00:19:25,480
Don't carry this burden on your own!

362
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:27,720
Like I told you five years ago,

363
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:28,940
You're not alone!

364
00:19:29,340 --> 00:19:30,880
I'm always here for you!

365
00:19:31,100 --> 00:19:32,660
All of your sadness and your hate!

366
00:19:33,220 --> 00:19:34,820
Let me carry all of it for you!

367
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:36,600
If you're lost, I'll find you!

368
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:39,180
When something happens and it's too much,

369
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:40,580
Please come to me!

370
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:41,900
Give it all to me!

371
00:19:42,060 --> 00:19:42,520
Everything!

372
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:43,260
It's okay!

373
00:19:43,500 --> 00:19:44,600
I'll take all of it!

374
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:45,860
Do you hear me?

375
00:19:46,260 --> 00:19:46,580
Okay?

376
00:19:47,300 --> 00:19:49,540
Don't let despair take you over, Origami!

377
00:19:49,720 --> 00:19:53,660
No matter how many worlds you try to break,

378
00:19:53,660 --> 00:19:55,480
I'll fight to get to you!

379
00:19:56,160 --> 00:19:57,600
I know you're in despair!

380
00:19:58,120 --> 00:20:00,640
I'll never stop trying to help you save yourself!

381
00:20:01,520 --> 00:20:02,760
Shiro...

382
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:04,600
My friend...

383
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:05,600
Come on!

384
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:06,860
Reach out to me, will ya?

385
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:08,860
I won't lose you!

386
00:20:21,360 --> 00:20:22,040
Origami!

387
00:20:23,660 --> 00:20:29,440
I...

388
00:20:29,440 --> 00:20:32,400
Thank you, Shiro.

389
00:20:33,960 --> 00:20:35,800
If you hadn't been here for me,

390
00:20:36,620 --> 00:20:38,520
I would have ended up doing something else

391
00:20:38,520 --> 00:20:40,400
I'd never be able to take back.

392
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:44,740
The fact that I killed my mom and dad

393
00:20:44,740 --> 00:20:46,680
is never going to go away from me.

394
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:49,600
Nor will the sin of slaying the ones I did

395
00:20:49,600 --> 00:20:50,840
in the original world.

396
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:54,260
That will stay with me forever.

397
00:20:55,080 --> 00:20:56,020
Even if...

398
00:20:56,020 --> 00:20:58,440
If it's changed so that it never even happened.

399
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:01,840
Origami...

400
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:03,680
You're right.

401
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:05,900
Unfortunately, I think that's a burden

402
00:21:05,900 --> 00:21:07,180
you'll always have to bear.

403
00:21:07,180 --> 00:21:25,900
I feel like I need to apologize.

404
00:21:25,900 --> 00:21:29,760
The feelings I've had towards you weren't actually love.

405
00:21:30,060 --> 00:21:32,060
I got two feelings confused, I think.

406
00:21:32,440 --> 00:21:34,160
I felt I could rely on you.

407
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:37,380
But now I realize that when I lost my parents,

408
00:21:37,540 --> 00:21:39,660
I had no other choice but to cling to you.

409
00:21:40,940 --> 00:21:41,800
Well, I'm honored.

410
00:21:42,420 --> 00:21:44,520
But it took bravery to trust me.

411
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:46,560
So you're saved because of you.

412
00:21:48,060 --> 00:21:48,940
Shiro...

413
00:21:48,940 --> 00:21:50,660
Oh, yeah.

414
00:21:51,060 --> 00:21:52,280
I've got something of yours.

415
00:21:53,600 --> 00:21:55,000
And I need to give it back.

416
00:21:55,460 --> 00:21:56,860
I held more than tears.

417
00:21:57,580 --> 00:21:58,260
Wouldn't you say?

418
00:21:58,260 --> 00:22:12,260
Shiro, do we...

419
00:22:12,260 --> 00:22:12,540
Oh!

420
00:22:12,540 --> 00:22:13,040
Oh!

421
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:13,340
Oh!

422
00:22:28,260 --> 00:22:39,440
Good grief, man.

423
00:22:39,680 --> 00:22:41,120
We'll never learn our limits.

424
00:22:41,580 --> 00:22:42,480
Or so I hope.

425
00:22:50,040 --> 00:22:53,440
Good morning, Shiro.

426
00:22:54,440 --> 00:22:56,020
Morning, Origami.

427
00:22:56,020 --> 00:23:00,180
Here, I have something to wipe your tears with.

428
00:23:00,380 --> 00:23:01,000
Thank you.

429
00:23:03,260 --> 00:23:03,820
What?

430
00:23:04,340 --> 00:23:05,900
Origami, what are you doing?

431
00:23:07,940 --> 00:23:09,120
School swimsuit.

432
00:23:09,840 --> 00:23:11,560
It retains moisture well.

433
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:17,140
Oh, I picked these up for you, too.

434
00:23:17,560 --> 00:23:19,080
Okay, I'm a little confused

435
00:23:19,080 --> 00:23:20,260
because when all that happened,

436
00:23:20,380 --> 00:23:22,540
didn't you say you never loved me to begin with?

437
00:23:23,260 --> 00:23:25,780
Yeah, which means our real love story

438
00:23:25,780 --> 00:23:26,880
can start now.

439
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:30,040
You better stay away from Shiro!

440
00:23:30,320 --> 00:23:31,300
Get off him!

441
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:32,400
Yes!

442
00:23:33,500 --> 00:23:33,840
Yuck!

443
00:23:33,980 --> 00:23:34,360
Hey!

444
00:23:34,480 --> 00:23:34,540
Yes!

445
00:23:47,400 --> 00:23:47,860
Hey!

446
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:48,060
Ooh!

447
00:23:48,440 --> 00:23:49,280
Hey!

448
00:23:49,340 --> 00:23:49,720
Hey!

449
00:23:49,920 --> 00:23:50,240
Hey!

450
00:23:50,360 --> 00:23:50,540
Say what!

451
00:23:51,280 --> 00:23:51,700
Hey!

452
00:23:51,800 --> 00:23:52,220
Hey!

453
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:53,300
Hey!

